  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "conjugate the most common irregular verbs in the preterite (ser, ir, hacer, tener, estar, decir and more)",
        "spot the three families of irregular stems (u, i and j) and their special endings",
        "write the forms without accents, as irregular preterites require",
        "know when a verb changes its meaning in the preterite (saber, conocer, querer, poder)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. How irregular preterites work"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Irregular verbs in the preterite change their <b>stem</b> and use their own set of endings. These endings have <b>no written accents</b> and the yo and él forms end in <b>-e</b> and <b>-o</b>, not <i>-é</i> and <i>-ó</i>."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.0,
        3.0,
        4.0,
        5.0
      ],
      "head": [
        "Person",
        "Ending",
        "Example: tener",
        "Example: decir"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "-e",
          "tuve",
          "dije"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "-iste",
          "tuviste",
          "dijiste"
        ],
        [
          "él / ella / usted",
          "-o",
          "tuvo",
          "dijo"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros / nosotras",
          "-imos",
          "tuvimos",
          "dijimos"
        ],
        [
          "vosotros / vosotras",
          "-isteis",
          "tuvisteis",
          "dijisteis"
        ],
        [
          "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
          "-ieron",
          "tuvieron",
          "dijeron (-eron after j)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "The same endings for every family below",
      "text": "Learn this one set of endings once. Then you only have to memorise the <b>stem</b> of each verb. Compare with the regular preterite (PDF 1): there yo ends in <b>-é</b> / <b>-í</b> and él in <b>-ó</b> / <b>-ió</b>, with accents."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        2.8,
        8.4,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "Family",
        "Verbs and stems",
        "Endings"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "u-stem",
          "estar estuv- · tener tuv- · poder pud- · poner pus- · saber sup- · andar anduv- · caber cup-",
          "-e -iste -o -imos -isteis -ieron"
        ],
        [
          "i-stem",
          "hacer hic- · querer quis- · venir vin-",
          "-e -iste -o -imos -isteis -ieron"
        ],
        [
          "j-stem",
          "decir dij- · traer traj- · conducir conduj- · traducir traduj- · producir produj-",
          "-e -iste -o -imos -isteis -eron"
