          "Special",
          "ser / ir fu- · dar d- · ver v-",
          "see section 2"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "2. Ser and ir: identical forms"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "<b>Ser</b> (to be) and <b>ir</b> (to go) have exactly the same forms in the preterite. The context tells you which verb it is: <b>ir</b> is followed by <b>a</b> + a place, <b>ser</b> by a noun or an adjective."
    },
    {
      "type": "conj",
      "tense": "preterite",
      "verb": "ser",
      "meaning": "to be",
      "label": "irregular verb · same forms as ir",
      "forms": [
        "*fu*i",
        "*fu*iste",
        "*fu*e",
        "*fu*imos",
        "*fu*isteis",
        "*fu*eron"
      ],
      "examples": [
        [
          "Fui camarero durante un verano.",
          "I was a waiter for one summer."
        ],
        [
          "¿Fuiste buen estudiante?",
          "Were you a good student?"
        ],
        [
          "El concierto fue un éxito.",
          "The concert was a success."
        ],
        [
          "Fuimos compañeros de piso.",
          "We were flatmates."
        ],
        [
          "¿Fuisteis amigos de niños?",
          "Were you (all) friends as children?"
        ],
        [
          "Los exámenes fueron difíciles.",
          "The exams were difficult."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "conj",
      "tense": "preterite",
      "verb": "ir",
      "meaning": "to go",
      "label": "irregular verb · same forms as ser",
      "forms": [
        "*fu*i",
        "*fu*iste",
        "*fu*e",
        "*fu*imos",
        "*fu*isteis",
        "*fu*eron"
      ],
      "examples": [
        [
          "Fui a Barcelona en tren.",
          "I went to Barcelona by train."
        ],
        [
          "¿Fuiste al gimnasio ayer?",
          "Did you go to the gym yesterday?"
        ],
        [
          "Ella fue a la farmacia.",
          "She went to the chemist's."
        ],
        [
          "Fuimos al cine el sábado.",
          "We went to the cinema on Saturday."
        ],
        [
          "¿Fuisteis a la playa?",
          "Did you (all) go to the beach?"
        ],
        [
          "Mis amigos fueron a Italia.",
          "My friends went to Italy."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "warn",
      "title": "No accent on one-syllable forms",
      "text": "<b>fui, fue, vi, vio, di, dio</b> have one syllable, so they never take a written accent. Writing <i>fuí</i>, <i>fué</i> or <i>vió</i> is a very common spelling mistake (older texts still use it)."
    },
